cammap is two things, and only one of them is licensed for reuse: the
record of cameras is, the code that draws it is not. They are separated
here because the site's whole purpose is that the record be cited,
plotted and built on, while the code is the maintainers' own.

  THE DATA   The Open Database License 1.0, below. The record of
             cameras: data/cameras.csv, data/points.js,
             backend/seed.sql, and any download of the same record the
             site offers (a CSV or GeoJSON of the cameras is the same
             data in another form).

  THE CODE   Not licensed. Everything in this repository that is not
             the record - the HTML pages, frontend/, tools/, backend/
             schema.sql and migrations/, the stylesheet - is
             Copyright (c) 2026 cammap contributors, all rights
             reserved. It is published where anyone can read it, and
             GitHub's own terms let you view and fork a public
             repository there; nothing here grants more than that.
             (lib/ and fonts/ are vendored third-party work under
             their own licences, unchanged, and are not ours to
             license either way.)

The copyright holder is named as "cammap contributors" because the
site puts no names on itself, on principle, and its licence should not
be the one place it does.


======================================================================
THE DATA: Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0
======================================================================

The record of facial recognition cameras published by cammap - the
contents of data/cameras.csv, data/points.js and backend/seed.sql, and
every download of that record the site offers in another format - is
made available under the Open Database License 1.0:

    https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/

You are free to copy, distribute, use, modify and build on the record,
including commercially, provided that you:

  attribute   say where it came from, in the form below;
  share-alike if you publish a database built on it, publish that
              under this licence too;
  keep open   if you distribute it under technical restriction, also
              offer a copy without.

The attribution to use:

    Contains data from cammap (https://forrest404.github.io/cammap/),
    made available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0.

The record was itself assembled from public sources - the Metropolitan
Police's published LFR deployment records, the British Transport
Police's deployment register, and named press reporting - and nothing
in it is estimated. Each entry's note and source say which. Reusing
the record does not remove the need to credit those sources where your
own use calls for it.

ODbL was chosen over CC BY-SA because this is a database, queried and
joined, rather than a document, read and quoted; it is the licence
OpenStreetMap uses for the same reason, and the map's own base tiles
come from OpenStreetMap data under it.
